## Pull requests

Templates: [.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE/](../../.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE/). Procedures: [`$git-commit` § Pull request](../skills/git-commit/procedures.md#pull-request). Branch order: [AGENTS.md § Change workflow](../../AGENTS.md#change-workflow) · **`$agent-workflow`**.

### Choose a template

| Template | Use when |
|----------|----------|
| [lite.md](../../.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE/lite.md) | Small PRs: docs-only, single-file chores, tiny fixes, low risk |
| [full.md](../../.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE/full.md) | Multi-package work, tokens/registry/cli, UI + template sync, breaking changes, or architectural impact |

When unsure, use `full.md`.

### Base branch

**Default PR target is `dev`, not `main`.** Do not touch **`main`** unless the user explicitly requests it. Use `--base dev` when the user does not specify a base.

### Before opening a PR

- [`$monorepo-verify-gate` § Format gate](../skills/monorepo-verify-gate/SKILL.md#format-gate-mandatory--blocks-git-write) — **`verify passed`** before `gh pr create`.
- Inspect vs `dev` per [procedures § Pull request](../skills/git-commit/procedures.md#pull-request).
- Push only when the user explicitly requests it.

### Fill the template

1. Read the chosen template from `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE/`.
2. Replace HTML comments with content from **all commits** on the branch.
3. Check Scope and Change Type boxes that match the diff.
4. Complete Package Boundary, Registry/CLI, Token/Styling, and UI sections when touched; mark **Not applicable** otherwise.
5. Record verification commands and results in the Verification table.
6. Delete optional sections that do not apply.

PR title may differ from a single commit subject when the branch has multiple commits.

### Create the PR

**Create and labels are one atomic step** — see [procedures § Pull request steps 4–6](../skills/git-commit/procedures.md#pull-request). Do not treat `gh pr create` alone as done; apply labels in the same turn, then verify before returning the URL.

```bash
gh pr create --base dev --title "short pr title" --body-file path/to/filled-body.md
gh pr edit <number> --add-label "type:feat,area:ui,status:ready-for-review"
gh pr view <number> --json labels
```

Fix wrong base: `gh pr edit <number> --base dev`.

### GitHub labels (required — same turn as create)

Apply labels per [procedures § Pull request](../skills/git-commit/procedures.md#pull-request) steps 4–6. Label namespaces: [CONTRIBUTING.md § GitHub labels](../../docs/contributors/CONTRIBUTING.md). Manifest: [`.github/labels.yml`](../../.github/labels.yml).

**Always apply:**

| Label | When |
|-------|------|
| `type:*` | One — mirrors primary commit type |
| `area:*` | One or more — every primary surface touched (see [area mapping](#area-mapping)) |
| `status:ready-for-review` | Open PR complete and awaiting review — removed on merge ([repo-pr-automation.yml](../../.github/workflows/repo-pr-automation.yml)) |
| `meta:breaking-change` | Public API, registry install paths, token CSS, or config breaks |
| `meta:changeset` | Changeset-only prep PR for an upcoming release (optional) |

**Label budget (max 4):** 1× `type:*`, up to 2× `area:*`, 1× `status:*`, optional 1× `meta:*`. Do not exceed — automation comments when count > 4.

**Do not apply on PRs:** `priority:*`, `automation:*`, `meta:good-first-issue`, `meta:help-wanted`, `meta:release-train` (bot applies on `dev` → `main` and sync PRs).

### area mapping

| Label | Paths / trigger |
|-------|-----------------|
| `area:ui` | `packages/ui/**` |
| `area:tokens` | `packages/tokens/**` |
| `area:registry` | `packages/registry/**` |
| `area:cli` | `packages/cli/**` |
| `area:playground` | `apps/playground/**` |
| `area:docs` | `docs/**`, `AGENTS.md`, package READMEs when docs-heavy |
| `area:repo` | Root tooling, `turbo.json`, workspace scripts, `.github/**` |
| `area:agents` | `.cursor/skills/**`, [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) |

Pick **all areas** that match the diff.

#### Label examples

| PR shape | Labels |
|----------|--------|
| UI-only feature | `type:feat`, `area:ui`, `status:ready-for-review` |
| UI + registry sync | `type:feat`, `area:ui`, `area:registry`, `status:ready-for-review` |
| Docs-only | `type:docs`, `area:docs`, `status:ready-for-review` |
| Agent workflow / git skill | `type:docs`, `area:agents`, `status:ready-for-review` |

```bash
gh pr edit <number> --add-label "type:feat,area:ui,area:registry,status:ready-for-review"
```

